From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 05 Nov 2026 21:30:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: release monitor DMA rings during pdev cleanup

RXDMA monitor setup allocates destination and descriptor rings, but pdev
SRNG cleanup only releases the monitor buffer ring. Release both missing
rings on teardown and setup failure. Unallocated or previously freed rings
are already ignored by ath11k_dp_srng_cleanup().

On IPQ9554, the missing frees retain 26 CMA pages (104 KiB) on each AHB
driver unload. The two allocations are 65543 and 32775 bytes, respectively.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -701,6 +701,8 @@
 	}
 
 	ath11k_dp_srng_cleanup(ab, &dp->rxdma_mon_buf_ring.refill_buf_ring);
+	ath11k_dp_srng_cleanup(ab, &dp->rxdma_mon_dst_ring);
+	ath11k_dp_srng_cleanup(ab, &dp->rxdma_mon_desc_ring);
 }
 
 void ath11k_dp_pdev_reo_cleanup(struct ath11k_base *ab)
